{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNBHQtSdPeiKZchopdL8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015vhXD4aqBoDkEcbo6BhRQq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/proposal.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"Each warning lists what the job can reach, including `~/.ard`\"\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a,\"**Default agent image under the local executor (#244, part of #55).** `ard serve` and `ard config check` read the host setting `ARD_AGENT_IMAGE`: a digest-pinned reference (`<name>@sha256:<64 hex>`) or a local image ID (`sha256:<hex>` from `make agent-image`); tags are refused (`executor.CheckImageRef`, `ErrImageRef`), and an invalid value stops startup. When it is set, `Prepare` runs every job that reads untrusted input and has no `Dockerfile` (triage, worker agent, test and fix steps, reviewer, and LLM scanner jobs) under Docker in that image, with the same flags and mounts as a Dockerfile role (`--cap-drop ALL`, `no-new-privileges`, worktree at `/work`, role directory `:ro`, and so on). A role's own `Dockerfile` wins. Deterministic scanners (trusted input) stay on the host. A local image is used as is; a digest that is not present is pulled. There is no fallback to host mode: `ard serve` runs `docker version` at startup and fails if Docker is down, and a job whose Docker setup fails at `Prepare` fails there. The controller's clone is not mounted, so `git` has no repository inside the container; every Docker job gets `GOFLAGS=-buildvcs=false` so `go build` does not fail on VCS stamping. Unset keeps today's behaviour. With it set, `ard config check` and `ard serve` no longer log or record `executor.host_untrusted` for roles it covers, and the hint of the warning names `ARD_AGENT_IMAGE`. \"+a,1)\ns=s.replace(\"| the role's `Dockerfile` image under Docker if it has one, else a host subprocess; hard timeout |\",\"| the role's `Dockerfile` image under Docker if it has one, else the `ARD_AGENT_IMAGE` default image when set and the role reads untrusted input, else a host subprocess; hard timeout |\",1)\ns=s.replace(\"without one the local executor runs a host subprocess and the Kubernetes\",\"without one the local executor runs a host subprocess (or, with `ARD_AGENT_IMAGE` set, a role that reads untrusted input runs in that image) and the Kubernetes\",1)\ns=s.replace(\"It is never published, to a public registry or to GHCR,\",\"The local executor uses it through `ARD_AGENT_IMAGE` (set to its image ID or a digest). It is never published, to a public registry or to GHCR,\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit -c core.excludesFile=/dev/null status --porcelain --untracked-files=all; git diff --stat | tail -1"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9602,"cache_read_input_tokens":55408,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9602},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3afce4d9-1589-41c9-9210-5171e088cc85","uuid":"fee4797e-8ada-4d42-85f8-3176dce294a0","timestamp":"2026-11-24T17:51:46.790Z","request_id":"req_011ChNBHQi2V2wNf7dNSWa72"}
