{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNBJRCL3bBNXgyTZ5C5X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Roles that read untrusted input and have no Dockerfile now run in the `ARD_AGENT_IMAGE` image under Docker, with no fallback to host mode. `go vet` and `go test ./internal/...` pass offline. I did not run `make lint` or the golangci-lint config. `make lint`'s gofmt step would flag a broken fixture under `internal/roles/testdata`, which I didn't touch. The Docker integration test and the live Mac check still need a person.\n\nI followed the owner's decision: the controller's clone is not mounted. Git is unavailable inside the container, and `GOFLAGS=-buildvcs=false` is set so `go build` doesn't fail on VCS stamping. That flag applies to every Docker job, including Dockerfile roles, so the flags stay identical.\n\n- **Validation:** `executor.CheckImageRef` accepts only `<name>@sha256:<64 hex>` or a local `sha256:<hex>` ID. Tags, leading `-`, and whitespace are rejected with `ErrImageRef`. `local.New`, `ard serve` and `ard config check` all use it.\n- **Local executor:**\n  - Precedence: `Prepare` uses the default image for untrusted-input jobs without a Dockerfile. A role's own Dockerfile wins, trusted scanners stay on the host, and unset behaves as before.\n  - Image availability: a local image is used as is, and a digest that isn't present locally is pulled.\n  - Failure: any Docker failure fails `Prepare`, and I tested that no worktree is left behind.\n- **Startup:** `ard serve` runs `docker version` when the setting is set and refuses to start if Docker is down.\n- **Warning:** `executor.host_untrusted` is no longer logged or recorded for covered roles, and the warning's hint now names `ARD_AGENT_IMAGE`. Config check and serve skip it through a new `HostUntrustedWith`.\n- **Tests and docs:** I added tests for each of the above (a fake docker binary for the executor cases). `docs/proposal.md` documents the setting, the precedence, the no-fallback rule, the missing clone mount and the warning change.\n\nA maintainer should review the no-fallback path closely, since it decides container versus host isolation. The report is in `.ard/244/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1037,"cache_read_input_tokens":66390,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1037},"output_tokens":746,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3afce4d9-1589-41c9-9210-5171e088cc85","uuid":"40460f54-9f62-45cc-b9c7-d5323782195e","timestamp":"2026-11-24T17:51:58.839Z","request_id":"req_011ChNBJR3tJrHGjXnCnoS8N"}
